<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <p role="eyebrow">Illustrated viewpoints—not real biographies</p>
      <h2>The same years did not feel the same to everyone</h2>
      <p font-size="lg"><b>People did not have equal rights or choices.</b></p>
      <grid image-aspect="square" image-shape="circle" spacing="medium">
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="square" prompt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative free market seller named Rosa in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult woman with medium-brown skin beside a simple produce basket and market cloth, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, restrained thoughtful expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons"/>
          <h4>Rosa</h4>
          <p font-size="sm"><b>Free market seller</b></p>
          <p>She watches for changes to trade.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="square" prompt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative rural worker named Tomás in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult man with tan skin beside a travel bag and food sack, historically grounded but non-specific work clothing, calm serious expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons"/>
          <h4>Tomás</h4>
          <p font-size="sm"><b>Rural worker</b></p>
          <p>He thinks about work, food, and travel.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="square" prompt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative enslaved worker named Luzia in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult Black woman standing with dignity beside folded cloth and a carrying basket, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, restrained direct expression, warm cream paper background, no chains, no violence, no text, no weapons"/>
          <h4>Luzia</h4>
          <p font-size="sm"><b>Enslaved worker</b></p>
          <p>She has far fewer rights and choices. The revolt does not end slavery.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15">
          <ai-image image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" aspect-ratio="square" prompt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative child named Davi in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, brown-skinned child listening while nearby adult hands hold an opened letter with no readable writing, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, curious restrained expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons"/>
          <h4>Davi</h4>
          <p font-size="sm"><b>Child</b></p>
          <p>He hears news shaped by the adults around him.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>